# React Native Starter Kit Development Guidelines

# General Code Style & Formatting
- Use functional and declarative programming patterns; avoid classes
- All services should export both named functions and a default combined export
- Use TypeScript for all files with proper types and interfaces
- Prefer iteration and modularization over code duplication
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError)

# Project Structure & Architecture
- Follow the folder structure pattern:
  - app/(app) - Main app screens
  - app/(auth) - Authentication screens
  - components - Reusable UI components
  - context - React context providers
  - services - Core business logic and services
  - hooks - Custom React hooks
  - translations - Language files
  - types - TypeScript types

# Styling & UI
- Use NativeWind (Tailwind CSS) for styling components
- Implement responsive design with Flexbox
- Ensure high accessibility (a11y) standards using native accessibility props

# Data & Form Handling
- Use react-hook-form with yup for form handling
- Wrap service functions in try-catch blocks with proper error handling
- Keep UI components pure when possible
- Use Firebase services for backend functionality

# Internationalization
- Never hardcode strings, always use i18n.t() for translations
- Organize translation keys by feature or screen
- Support multiple languages with proper fallbacks

# TypeScript Best Practices
- Avoid any and enums; use explicit types instead
- Create interfaces for all component props
- Enable strict mode in TypeScript config
- Use type guards for conditional logic 